      "category": "ai",
      "title": "Born Against, or why hobby programming communities are against LLM usage",
      "url": "https://blog.fogus.me/llm/born-against.html",
      "discuss_url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49187061",
      "score": 252,
      "comments": 226,
      "author": "lladnar",
      "published": "2026-08-05T18:37:49Z",
      "bullets": [
        "Hobby developers reject AI tools like GitHub Copilot to preserve intrinsic problem-solving, skill acquisition, and deep conceptual learning in programming.",
        "LLM-generated code increases review burden on open-source maintainers due to subtle bugs, security vulnerabilities, and unverified, low-quality PR submissions.",
        "Licensing ambiguities surrounding model training data create intellectual property and GPL/MIT compliance concerns within collaborative developer communities."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "lobsters",
      "subsource": "lobste.rs/programming",
      "category": "engineering",
      "title": "Faster Than Ninja",
      "url": "https://build2.org/blog/faster-than-ninja.xhtml",
