      "score": 48,
      "comments": 4,
      "author": "borisk",
      "published": "2026-08-05T10:37:51Z",
      "bullets": [
        "Alternative build tools like n2 and samurai outperform Ninja using Rust, zero-copy parsing, and reduced heap allocations for build graphs.",
        "Incremental build speed depends heavily on optimizing OS stat call latency, mtime caching, and minimal-overhead dependency graph evaluation.",
        "Replacing traditional build graph processing with thread-pool-driven DAG execution cuts no-op build times down to sub-millisecond ranges."
      ]
    },
    {
