      "author": "kevincox",
      "published": "2026-08-04T18:31:48Z",
      "bullets": [
        "Defending complex systems requires asymmetric effort; implementation flaws in IAM, TLS, or memory management repeatedly invalidate upper-layer controls.",
        "Secure-by-default architectures and paved roads mitigate human error far more effectively than manual code reviews or reactive patching.",
        "Modern application security demands automated SBOM tracking and strict dependency pinning to mitigate compounding supply chain attack vectors."
      ]
    },
